                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                        "entry_id": "37b31add-3a1a-37ce-bd9e-b53b2d2811a9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "небольшая соломенная шляпа с круглыми полями"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "532044f8-463a-40f4-8aea-7704548eec46",
                                "sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                                "text": "Старик был великолепен в новой парусиновой пиджачной паре, украинской вышитой сорочке и твёрдой соломенной шляпе канотье."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0d1f5a7-0b0d-45ce-ae2b-276913bc54af",
                                "sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                                "text": "О́блую громаду в полосатом трико ущипнул краб, и обладательница громады млеет, полагая, что это рука соседа — щуплого щёголя в канотье."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5434ab59-1c5a-44a5-9a5c-0718b7ee9bfe",
                                "sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                                "text": "Размахивая газетами, канотье и панамскими шляпами, старики затрусили по мостовой."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb3c3ab6-835e-4d9d-9715-5a57fd5561de",
                        "source_entry_id": "37b31add-3a1a-37ce-bd9e-b53b2d2811a9",
                        "source_sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                        "target_lang_word": "boater",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "boater",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22545c5c-860c-3162-af5a-d725dfcb0ea9",
                                        "entry_id": "6bea6991-ae98-38f4-8e74-5d9c019746eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who travels by boat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "049b5789-cb72-3058-ae08-0633d058b25d",
                                        "entry_id": "6bea6991-ae98-38f4-8e74-5d9c019746eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of boatman, particularly its captain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bbda11a-6442-4532-a59f-75f8fde2b321",
                                                "sense_id": "049b5789-cb72-3058-ae08-0633d058b25d",
                                                "text": "In the summer of 1992, eight beaches were closed and swimmers were warned away because of colliform bacteria, caused by boaters emptying toilets directly into the lake or onto nearby shores. Park officials may soon supply the lake with floating waste disposal systems."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94347d75-b821-3be8-a915-1cdf13eabeec",
                                        "entry_id": "6bea6991-ae98-38f4-8e74-5d9c019746eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A straw hat, very stiff, with a flat brim and crown."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "284ed7db-4f14-4648-8821-d0cbf586d46f",
                                                "sense_id": "94347d75-b821-3be8-a915-1cdf13eabeec",
                                                "text": "Technically, Melania Trump was in attendance, but she chose to make herself almost invisible. Her dark boater hat was worn so low that it threw her entire face into shadow, and made eye contact with cameras or guests impossible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0cbfde17-da61-447d-acf1-45f3379f8326",
                        "source_entry_id": "37b31add-3a1a-37ce-bd9e-b53b2d2811a9",
                        "source_sense_id": "acad9d99-acb4-336e-bbf4-16582b3f0ceb",
                        "target_lang_word": "basher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "basher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b3f0c17-e974-333b-92f1-e6cd5cb2363c",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who bashes something, figuratively or literally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c74ad622-7255-4ad4-a12b-e80d0dd22709",
                                                "sense_id": "6b3f0c17-e974-333b-92f1-e6cd5cb2363c",
                                                "text": "Consider the cold-eyed thrush, that springy carnivore of lawns, worm stabber, basher to death of snails."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91f3cae7-2bd7-3f76-90f0-9887838447c7",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who engages in gratuitous physical or verbal attacks on a group or type of people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cb1e9df-c5e3-46b6-a67a-97bf289dffd3",
                                                "sense_id": "91f3cae7-2bd7-3f76-90f0-9887838447c7",
                                                "text": "a Paki-basher"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "239b22e0-4947-4bf6-bc00-50f866b33d64",
                                                "sense_id": "91f3cae7-2bd7-3f76-90f0-9887838447c7",
                                                "text": "He was beaten up by a queer-basher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c2388f6-a572-46cb-a228-b1ba0e062aa0",
                                                "sense_id": "91f3cae7-2bd7-3f76-90f0-9887838447c7",
                                                "text": "It's impossible to count how many harassers and bashers are growing discouraged at the sight of 12 or so queers in black and teal uniforms walking down the street in tight formation. The message is simple: queer folk are banding together and walking the streets in cities around the United States to protect their own."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fafef238-27a3-3228-b36d-73f5b8c0ff9c",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A trainspotter, especially one who likes to travel on specific trains or trainlines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78332608-3d0c-42d2-82f3-94060f57e61f",
                                                "sense_id": "fafef238-27a3-3228-b36d-73f5b8c0ff9c",
                                                "text": "There are bashers and bashers, of course. Most of them, like 'Bob', try to travel as far as possible behind a particular type of locomotive. 'Bob' likes Class 37 diesels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8315fb08-ffd6-4582-a704-e338c991c1ba",
                                                "sense_id": "fafef238-27a3-3228-b36d-73f5b8c0ff9c",
                                                "text": "Nose around any modest-sized station and the odds are you'll find that the chargeman's office doubles as a bashers' club, a place where shivering spotters can get warm and catch up on the gen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21e8ddd3-ec51-4dbe-b7de-05967a729104",
                                                "sense_id": "fafef238-27a3-3228-b36d-73f5b8c0ff9c",
                                                "text": "Determined 'bashers' do still ride trains, of course, seeking to cram the largest number of route-miles into 24 hours."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c97b4188-237b-35e7-af10-8e1efcc0e758",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rainproof sheet for sleeping under."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "918815fc-778c-4b06-9a7b-2dbbdf4438d4",
                                                "sense_id": "c97b4188-237b-35e7-af10-8e1efcc0e758",
                                                "text": "Suddenly awake she looked around, startled, it was light, hot, intensely hot and she was sleeping in a shell scrape under a basher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "305beeee-91c0-40a0-8f9f-311fdca93403",
                                                "sense_id": "c97b4188-237b-35e7-af10-8e1efcc0e758",
                                                "text": "I was well used to sleeping out under the stars whatever the weather. I had a hammock and a basher, a rain sheet to go over where I was sleeping."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2809157c-be17-3076-85f8-98393a368697",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shelter built from improvised materials by a homeless person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8ea231a-c6cc-3c7f-b4fa-7d4fb8c8d631",
                                        "entry_id": "d4a8c09e-7691-3a5e-9fa7-a24b9040df4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of small floodlight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43fa886d-903a-41a8-9000-0741cefb0e67",
                        "source_entry_id": "37b31add-3a1a-37ce-bd9e-b53b2d2811a9",
